# CR 702.85a, 709.3, 709.3b: cascade exiles Life // Death (mana value 3 as the card, under Bloodbraid Challenger's 4) and its
# controller casts one half of it for free: the spell cast is that half, not the card. Both halves (Life 1, Death 2) are under 4,
# but Death needs a creature card in a graveyard to target and there is none, so only Life can be cast and nothing is asked
# (the refusal): a face that can't be cast is no choice (CR 709.3a). Life makes lands 1/1 creatures until end of turn. Cascade's own
# filter on the spell's mana value keeps a face over the limit out too; no card here has a face dearer than the card itself except
# a modal double-faced one, and none exists in the content.

